{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Scholarship Applications Summary",
  "subtitle": "Key metrics and trends for current scholarship applications",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Applications Received",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Approved Applications",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Approved'",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Rejection Rate",
    "sql": "SELECT ROUND(COUNT(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Rejected' THEN 1 END) * 100.0 / COUNT(*), 1) AS rejection_rate FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
    "unit": "%"
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Applications by District",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 20",
    "x": "district",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Applications by Category",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Category\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "category",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Monthly Application Trend",
    "sql": "SELECT TO_CHAR(\"DOB\", 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "month",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top 5 Schemes by Applications",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Name of scheme\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 5"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "Our board has received **{{p1}}** scholarship applications in total, with **{{p2}}** approved so far. The current rejection rate stands at **{{p3}}**, indicating a need for careful review processes. District-wise, **{{p4.x[0]}}** leads with **{{p4.y[0]}}** applications, while **{{p4.x[1]}}** follows closely. Category-wise, **{{p5.x[0]}}** applicants dominate the pool with **{{p5.y[0]}}** submissions. The monthly trend shows steady growth, with peaks in **{{p6.x[0]}}** and **{{p6.x[1]}}**. The most popular schemes are **{{p7.0[0]}}** and **{{p7.1[0]}}**, suggesting strong interest in these programs."
